{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_26","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n- **2307.12976, chunk 4 (pp. 10–12):** Error taxonomy separates no effect, abstention and wrong/noisy changes. Larger models help but do not solve ripple behavior. Limited to one edit and local graph; distant facts are not tested.\n- **2307.12976, chunk 5 (pp. 13–15):** References reviewed; useful links include CounterFact+, MQuAKE, ROME, MEMIT, and in-context editing. No additional experiments in this chunk.\n- **2401.07453, chunk 1 (pp. 1–3):** Sequential ROME/MEMIT/MEND/FT-C on GPT-2 XL and GPT-J, CounterFact. zsRE QA-to-completion mismatch motivates prompt-format controls. Four random 1k subsets for ROME, 2k for MEMIT.\n- **2401.07453, chunk 2 (pp. 4–6):** Distinguishes gradual loss from disabling edits. Tracks previously edited facts, neighborhood preference and balanced 200-example SST2/MRPC/NLI/CoLA F1. Layer-change norm spikes accompany collapse; tiny benchmark accuracy alone misses deterioration.\n- **2401.07453, chunk 3 (pp. 7–9):** MEMIT postpones collapse and retains more past edits but does not eliminate loss. Disabling single ROME edits can harm even fresh models. Findings about sequential scale are not a proof that every isolated edit leaks.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport requests,json,subprocess\nfrom bs4 import BeautifulSoup\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\np=Path('notes/paper_metadata.json');m=json.loads(p.read_text())\nfor i in ['2510.17941','2202.05262','2206.06520','2410.02355']:\n r=requests.get('https://arxiv.org/abs/'+i,timeout=60);r.raise_for_status();s=BeautifulSoup(r.text,'html.parser');r=requests.get('https://arxiv.org/pdf/'+i,timeout=120);r.raise_for_status();assert r.content.startswith(b'%PDF');f=Path('papers/'+i+'.pdf');f.write_bytes(r.content)\n m.append({'id':i,'title':s.find('meta',attrs={'name':'citation_title'})['content'],'authors':[x['content'] for x in s.find_all('meta',attrs={'name':'citation_author'})],'url':'https://arxiv.org/abs/'+i,'abstract':s.select_one('.abstract').get_text(' ',strip=True),'pages':len(PdfReader(f).pages)})\n subprocess.run(['.venv/bin/python','.codex/skills/paper-finder/scripts/pdf_chunker.py',str(f),'--pages-per-chunk','3'],capture_output=True,check=True)\np.write_text(json.dumps(m,indent=2));print([(x['id'],x['title'],x['pages']) for x in m])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
