{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n- **2410.21272, chunk 1 (pp. 1–3):** ICLR 2025; four pretrained models, single-token numbers and correctly answered prompts. Activation patching identifies arithmetic circuits; official technion-cs-nlp/llm-arithmetic-heuristics. Tested operators +, −, ×, integer division.\n- **2410.21272, chunk 2 (pp. 4–6):** Sparse late MLP neurons implement overlapping range/modulo/result-pattern heuristics; roughly 200 neurons per layer suffice for high circuit faithfulness. Mechanism suggests structured neighborhood tests rather than only adjacent sums.\n- **2410.21272, chunk 3 (pp. 7–9):** Matched ablations preferentially harm associated prompts; incomplete heuristics explain errors. Pythia checkpoint analysis finds gradual heuristic development. This is a circuit study, not an edit-isolation result.\n- **2410.21272, chunk 4 (pp. 10–12):** Explicit human-interpretation and single-token-number limitations; results need not transfer to digit-tokenized models or all arithmetic. References reviewed.\n- **2410.21272, chunk 5 (pp. 13–15):** Appendix faithfulness: addition .97 with six heads; subtraction .98; multiplication .90 with 20 heads. MLP0 enriches numeric embeddings; attention moves operand/operator information.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
