{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat > scripts/download_search_results.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport requests,json,concurrent.futures,time,re,hashlib\nfrom pypdf import PdfReader\nR=Path.cwd();assert (R/'.git').exists()\npapers=json.loads((R/'paper_search.json').read_text())['papers']\ndef fetch(item):\n i,x=item; out=dict(x,index=i);u=x['url'];pid='CorpusId:'+u.split('CorpusId:')[-1] if 'CorpusId:' in u else u.rsplit('/',1)[-1]\n try:\n  r=requests.get(f'https://api.semanticscholar.org/graph/v1/paper/{pid}',params={'fields':'title,externalIds,openAccessPdf'},timeout=30);r.raise_for_status();m=r.json();out['resolved']=m\n  aid=m.get('externalIds',{}).get('ArXiv');url=f'https://arxiv.org/pdf/{aid}' if aid else (m.get('openAccessPdf') or {}).get('url')\n  if not url:out['status']='no_open_pdf';return out\n  out['pdf_url']=url;p=R/'papers'/((aid or f'search_{i:03d}')+'.pdf')\n  if not p.exists():\n   r=requests.get(url,timeout=90);r.raise_for_status();assert r.content.startswith(b'%PDF'),'not PDF';p.write_bytes(r.content)\n  out.update(status='downloaded',file=str(p.relative_to(R)),pages=len(PdfReader(p).pages),sha256=hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest())\n except Exception as e:out.update(status='failed',error=str(e)[:250])\n return out\nwith concurrent.futures.ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=4) as pool:\n with (R/'notes/search_downloads.jsonl').open('w') as f:\n  for x in pool.map(fetch,enumerate(papers)):\n   f.write(json.dumps(x)+'\\\\n');f.flush();print(x['index'],x['status'],flush=True)\nPY\n.venv/bin/python scripts/download_search_results.py > notes/search_download_progress.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n- **2502.00873, chunk 1 (pp. 1–3):** GPT-J, Pythia-6.9B, Llama3.1-8B on all 10k additions with operands 0–99; single-token regime. Fits linear plus Fourier features (periods 2/5/10/100) to numerical states and tests via causal patching.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 2 (pp. 4–6):** Helix fits beat circular/polynomial controls and recover much of activation-patch effect. GPT-J attention transfers operand helices; middle MLPs construct answer representation, later layers read it out. Other operations are partly explained, not completely.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 3 (pp. 7–9):** Top neuron preactivations fit periodic functions; authors acknowledge the exact trigonometric computation is not isolated. Representation-level algorithm and neuron-level heuristics are not necessarily contradictory descriptions.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 4 (pp. 10–12):** References and appendix specify prompting, train/test split for helix fits, randomized controls and dimensional ablations. Strong model/prompt dependence argues for recording tokenizer and template.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
