{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n- **2502.00873, chunk 5 (pp. 13–15):** Prompted accuracies 80.5% GPT-J, 77.2% Pythia, 98% Llama3.1. Fourier and PCA diagnostics plus nonlinear-manifold experiment; Llama may use additional computation beyond GPT-J account.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 6 (pp. 16–18):** Out-of-sample helix fits, randomized controls, causal dimension ablation and attention-head analysis. Interventions can lower answer margins without changing top-1 accuracy—motivates distributional leakage metrics.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 7 (pp. 19–21):** Path patching supports distinct construction/readout stages; linear-number fit alone is insufficient. GPT-J errors often ±10; hypothesis tested against carry effects.\n- **2502.00873, chunk 8 (pp. 22–24):** Error asymmetry linked to periodic logits and bias toward smaller answers; carry explanation not supported. nnsight implementation; single 48GB A6000 reported. These are interpretive results on bounded additions.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
