{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_58","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat >> literature_review.md <<'EOF'\n\n### 2410.17194, chunks 1–3 (pp. 1–9)\nNishi et al., Representation Shattering in Transformers (ICML 2025): controlled 2-layer transformer learns walks over three cyclic graphs of 2,048 entities. ROME, MEMIT, PMET, AlphaEdit edits evaluated for direct recall, logical inference and compositional inference on edit/retain/test relations. Both corrective and counterfactual edits damage accuracy in this setup. Representation-distance distortion correlates with performance loss (reported r²=.905); larger graph edit distance increases distortion. Calendar edits in Llama3-8B and Mamba extend evidence beyond synthetic models. Authors explicitly do not claim a formal causal proof. These results motivate structural downstream tests but do not establish impossibility of isolated arithmetic edits.\nEOF\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
