ly.','files':[],'counts':dict(collections.Counter(r['stratum'] for r in rows))}\nfor s,rr in by_split.items():\n p=D/f'{s}.jsonl';p.write_text(''.join(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False)+'\\\\n' for r in rr));manifest['files'].append({'file':str(p.relative_to(R)),'rows':len(rr),'bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})\n(D/'manifest.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2));sample=[]\nfor st in manifest['counts']:sample.append(next(r for r in rows if r['stratum']==st))\n(R/'datasets/arithmetic_sample.json').write_text(json.dumps(sample,indent=2,ensure_ascii=False))\nprint(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2))\nPY\n.venv/bin/python scripts/build_arithmetic_suite.py\"","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-2d1a-codex-gpt-6-astra\n{\n  \"version\": 1,\n  \"seed\": null,\n  \"generation\": \"deterministic enumeration\",\n  \"counterfactual_rule\": \"Recursively evaluate AST; at each binary + node, if both evaluated operands equal 2 return 5; all other operations ordinary. Not a globally consistent arithmetic axiom system.\",\n  \"intentional_overlap\": \"Exact target 2+2= occurs in train and test efficacy only.\",\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"file\": \"datasets/arithmetic_isolation/train.jsonl\",\n      \"rows\": 405,\n      \"bytes\": 75589,\n      \"sha256\": \"50cb6ae7225964afee5d634b9b36a5c2083f4a6d4c52287155b0fc5dbd206fff\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"datasets/arithmetic_isolation/dev.jsonl\",\n      \"rows\": 115,\n      \"bytes\": 23423,\n      \"sha256\": \"8d203a83b5dab914e2ce06b331b3ba6f93717cc1cb1fc34a16cd28860e19dc73\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"file\": \"datasets/arithmetic_isolation/test.jsonl\",\n      \"rows\": 1879,\n      \"bytes\": 361123,\n      \"sha256\": \"f6c30a516c06844e92384ca3e080774788d6c8c1552cf78439c58001e9d9948e\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"counts\": {\n    \"target\": 1,\n    \"paraphrase\": 23,\n    \"efficacy\": 1,\n    \"replay\": 400,\n    \"arithmetic_dev\": 81,\n    \"near_addition\": 440,\n    \"far_addition\": 400,\n    \"other_operations\": 882,\n    \"lexical_near_miss\": 9,\n    \"semantic_notation\": 2,\n    \"downstream\": 75,\n    \"downstream_control\": 75,\n    \"downstream_word\": 2,\n    \"strategy_diagnostic\": 2,\n    \"robustness_diagnostic\": 6\n  }\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_69","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat > datasets/.gitignore <<'EOF'\n# Keep local data out of git; retain only reproducibility metadata and small examples.\n*\n\"'!.gitignore\n!README.md\n!*_sample.json\n!validation.json\n!control_validation.json\n!arithmetic_isolation/\narithmetic_isolation/*\n!arithmetic_isolation/manifest.json\nEOF\ncat > datasets/README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Datasets\n\nAll data are locally available. Large/raw files are excluded by this directory's \"'`.gitignore`; samples are below100KB. Download scripts use pinned revisions. Run from the repository root in the isolated environment:\n\n```bash\npwd\nuv sync\nuv run python scripts/download_datasets.py\nuv run python scripts/download_controls.py\nuv run python scripts/build_arithmetic_suite.py\n```\n\n## CounterFact (user-specified)\n\nSource: [azhx/counterfact](https://huggingface.co/datasets/azhx/counterfact), pinned revision `c01c413f856ee38f5c080c9fc5e87aff478e2ff9`; original benchmark from ROME. Local `counterfact/*.parquet`. Train19,728 and test2,191 records (21,919 total),12,387,190 compressed bytes. Seven fields: `case_id`, `pararel_idx`, structured `requested_rewrite` (prompt,subject,relation_id,target_true,target_new), and lists of paraphrase, neighborhood, attribute and generation prompts. No top-level nulls; all rewrites nonempty. Hashes and download URLs: `validation.json`; actual three-record sample: `counterfact_sample.json`.\n\nUse to measure factual-answer spillover under the arithmetic edit and optionally sanity-check existing editors. Preserve this mirror'\"'s splits; do not assume they match every paper's evaluation partition. It does not contain arithmetic edits and cannot replace the custom suite. The hosted card does not specify a data license; provenance is known but redistribution terms remain unresolved. A code repository's license is not automatically a dataset license.\n\n## GSM8K test\n\nSource: [official grade-school-math repository](https://github.com/openai/grade-school-math), commit \"'`3101c7d5072418e28b9008a6636bde82a006892c`. Local `gsm8k/test.jsonl`,1,319 examples. Fields `question` and `answer`; latter includes reasoning and a `####` final answer. All records parse, have nonempty questions and final-answer delimiters. Official repository MIT license saved locally in `gsm8k/LICENSE`. Only test split downloaded; never train on it. `gsm8k_sample.json` contains three actual examples.\n\nUse as math capability control, with a fixed answer parser. These problems may implicitly depend on2+2 and are not uniformly unrelated. Report overall accuracy and inspect changed items; do not score all counterfactual propagation as unrelated leakage.\n\n## WikiText-2 raw v1\n\nSource: [Salesforce/wikitext](https://huggingface.co/datasets/Salesforce/wikitext), revision `b08601e04326c79dfdd32d625aee71d232d685c3`. Local `wikitext2/{train,validation,test}.parquet`. Train36,718, validation3,760, test4,358 rows, single string field `text`. Empty lines and article headings are intentional; counts appear in `control_validation.json`. The card lists CC-BY-SA3.0 and GFDL. `wikitext2_sample.json` contains three nonblank test rows.\n\nTrain split can supply unrelated replay/preservation text; validation selects regularization/checkpoints; test is held out for NLL/KL only. Concatenate according to documented article boundaries and use identical tokenization/windows before and after editing. Drop blank rows consistently or preserve their separators; record the choice. This is a narrow text-distribution control, not proof that all unrelated behavior is preserved.\n\n## Arithmetic isolation suite (generated locally)\n\nGenerated by `scripts/build_arithmetic_suite.py`, no model/API dependency. Local `arithmetic_isolation/{train,dev,test}.jsonl`:405/115/1,879 records (2,399 total). `arithmetic_isolation/manifest.json` records hashes/counts and counterfactual semantics; `arithmetic_sample.json` contains one example per stratum. This new dataset is necessary because entity-relation editing benchmarks lack the required arithmetic strata. It is a deterministic pilot suite, not an established validated benchmark.\n\nSchema: `id`, `split`, `stratum`, `family`, `prompt`, `base_answer`, `edit_answer`; optional operands/operator, paired AST and `pair_id`, semantic diagnostic flags. Base labels use ordinary arithmetic. The edited AST oracle recursively evaluates each operation and returns5 when the evaluated operands of a binary addition are both2; all other operations use ordinary arithmetic. This is a local operational semantics, not consistent Peano arithmetic. Ordinary labels and edited-rule labels must be reported separately.\n\nTraining contains the exact target, four paraphrases and400 replay sums. Select target/paraphrase/replay strata deliberately; do not train every condition on all405 rows. Dev uses different wording and operands21–29; replay operands30–49; test near sums0–20 and far sums50–69. Test includes15 held-out target surfaces (including three translations),440 neighboring sums,400 distant sums,882 subtraction/multiplication controls, near misses, notation variants,60 dependent ASTs with60 matched nondependent controls, four stories, six robustness diagnostics and one exact efficacy query. Dev contains15 AST pairs. Numeric templates deliberately repeat across disjoint operand domains; semantic template independence is not claimed. Small language/word-problem strata are illustrative, not powered estimates.\n\nThe literal key occurs in both training and test efficacy by design; other cross-split prompt overlap is forbidden and checked. Held-out target wording must not enter training or generated documents. `strategy_diagnostic` stories can be solved by multiplication or addition; `semantic_gold_defined=false` means no unique edit-propagation gold. Robustness diagnostics have null labels. A truth-value query mentioning2+2 is a semantic dependency, even though its surface is a lexical near miss; do not put it in the preservation denominator. Copying/counting characters in the string are preservation tasks. Non-English and Unicode cases require tokenizer-aware baseline checks.\n\n## Loading and validation\n\n```python\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json\nimport pyarrow.parquet as pq\ncounterfact = pq.read_table(next(Path('\"'datasets/counterfact').glob('train-*.parquet')))\nwiki_test = pq.read_table('datasets/wikitext2/test.parquet')\ngsm8k = [json.loads(s) for s in Path('datasets/gsm8k/test.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\narithmetic = [json.loads(s) for s in Path('datasets/arithmetic_isolation/test.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]\n\"'```\n\nChecks cover file hashes, full parsing/row counts, required values, arithmetic oracle correctness, unique IDs and cross-split prompt overlap. They are data checks; no LLM has been evaluated. Re-run `scripts/validate_resources.py` after gathering is complete. Further experiment-time review should audit semantic categories, baseline-known items, answer formatting, and template correlations.\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python scripts/update_state.py <<'\"'EOF'\nPhases 1–2 complete. Literature:40 PDFs plus3 specified web articles; all specified papers and Shattering fully chunk-reviewed; access failures recorded. planning.md fixes three directions and pruning rationale. Data: pinned CounterFact21,919 records, GSM8K test1,319, WikiText-2 raw all3splits, generated arithmetic suite2,399 (405train/115dev/1,879test). Sources/hashes/checks and licenses in datasets/README.md, validation.json, control_validation.json, arithmetic_isolation/manifest.json; raw data ignored by git. Arithmetic labels distinguish ordinary arithmetic from a local recursive counterfactual rule; diagnostics are not universal gold.\nNext Phase 3: clone official FT, ROME/AlphaEdit, RippleEdits and SDF code; inspect README/dependencies/entrypoints and pin commits. Remaining limitations: supplemental PDF API failures; CounterFact data license unspecified; custom suite template correlation and small semantic strata; GPU/model access not yet tested. No model experiments performed.\nEOF\npwd; cat STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
