{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_78","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"pwd; cat > scripts/download_ripple.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport requests,json,hashlib\nR=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];assert Path.cwd()==R and (R/'.git').exists()\nD=R/'datasets/ripple_edits';D.mkdir(exist_ok=True);manifest=[]\nfor name in ['popular','random','recent']:\n url=f'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/edenbiran/RippleEdits/54f3b88af4895a3aacb580ec63ce7ae857185040/data/benchmark/{name}.json'\n p=D/(name+'.json');local=R/'code/RippleEdits/data/benchmark'/p.name\n if local.exists():data=local.read_bytes()\n else:\n  r=requests.get(url,timeout=120);r.raise_for_status();data=r.content\n p.write_bytes(data);rows=json.loads(data);assert isinstance(rows,list) and all('edit' in x for x in rows)\n manifest.append(dict(file=str(p.relative_to(R)),source=url,rows=len(rows),bytes=len(data),sha256=hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(),keys=sorted(rows[0])))\n if name=='popular':(R/'datasets/ripple_sample.json').write_text(json.dumps(rows[:1],indent=2))\n(R/'datasets/ripple_validation.json').write_text(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2));print(json.dumps(manifest,indent=2))\nPY\n.venv/bin/python scripts/download_ripple.py\ncat >> datasets/.gitignore <<'EOF'\n\"'!ripple_validation.json\nEOF\ncat >> datasets/README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n\n## RippleEdits (located during official code inspection)\n\nSource: [official repository](https://github.com/edenbiran/RippleEdits), commit \"'`54f3b88af4895a3aacb580ec63ce7ae857185040`. Reproduce from workspace root with `uv run python scripts/download_ripple.py`; the script uses pinned raw URLs or the identical local clone. Local `ripple_edits/{popular,random,recent}.json`; full counts/hashes/schema in `ripple_validation.json`, one actual edit in `ripple_sample.json`. These are strata rather than train/test splits. Each record has the edit and six conditional evaluation criteria, with acceptable answer aliases. Retain condition queries and explicit denominators when adapting evaluation. This provides a structural-edit comparison, not an additional research direction. The repository carries MIT licensing; facts derive from Wikidata, whose source-data terms also apply. Embedded upstream data remain in the untouched code clone; the experiment-ready copy is under datasets/.\nEOF\ncat > code/README.md <<'\"'EOF'\n# Official implementations\n\nSix shallow clones, unmodified. Readmes and dependency manifests inspected; relevant entrypoint signatures checked. No training or API generation was run. Exact commits are in \"'`notes/code_manifest.json`. Reproduce initially with `uv run python scripts/clone_repositories.py`; to reproduce the precise snapshot, fetch and checkout each manifest commit (default-branch heads can change). Keep dependencies isolated with uv; do not run upstream conda setup instructions. These are source references, not six installed working packages.\n\n| Repository / local directory | What to reuse | Entry points | Requirements and limitations |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| [model-editing-ft](https://github.com/au-revoir/model-editing-ft), `model-editing-ft/` | Answer-token masking, paraphrase/replay loss and single-edit trainer for direction1 | `single_edit/run.py` main/train, `single_edit/trainer.py` CustomCollatorWithPadding/Trainer, `single_edit/data.py`; mass edit `run.py`, `trainer.py` | Original Python3.9.11, torch1.13+cu117, transformers4.31 dev, PEFT0.4 dev, custom bundled TRL. NumPy1.22/SciPy1.7 pins incompatible with fresh Python3.12; port minimal loss/data logic or separate uv environment. Augmented mass datasets and TFIDF artifacts are separate downloads and not needed for the arithmetic pilot. No root LICENSE found. |\n| [RippleEdits](https://github.com/edenbiran/RippleEdits), `RippleEdits/` | Six-axis conditional ripple evaluation, in-context baseline, fact preservation controls | `src/evaluation.py` Evaluator/ConditionsEvaluator, `src/modeleditor.py` ModelEditor, `src/queryexecutor.py` QueryExecutor, `src/build_benchmark.py` | Python3.9, torch2.0.1+cu118, transformers4.31, datasets2.14, old OpenAI client. Model/GPU requirements depend on executor. MIT. Released benchmark copied to datasets/ and validated; no need to regenerate through live Wikidata. |\n| [ROME](https://github.com/kmeng01/rome), `rome/` | Rank-one parametric comparator and CounterFact evaluation | `rome/rome_main.py` apply_rome_to_model, `experiments/evaluate.py`, `notebooks/rome.ipynb`, `rome/layer_stats.py` | README supports GPT2-XL/GPT-J, GPU-only, torch/HF. Requires model-specific second moments, subject spans and layer config. MIT. Check current r-ROME fixes before interpreting collapse as intrinsic; no current-fix validation performed. |\n| [AlphaEdit](https://github.com/jianghoucheng/AlphaEdit), `AlphaEdit/` | Preservation-aware null-space comparator within direction1 | `AlphaEdit/AlphaEdit_main.py` apply_AlphaEdit_to_model, `experiments/evaluate.py`, `hparams/AlphaEdit/` | README: at least A40 48GB, torch2.6, transformers4.51.3, datasets2.21; Llama3-8B examples need weights/access and covariance data. MIT. Null-space guarantee concerns sampled key matrices, not every possible prompt. |\n| [false-facts](https://github.com/safety-research/false-facts), `false-facts/` | Original SDF universe/document generation, fine-tuning and belief evaluation | `false_facts/synth_doc_generation.py`, `false_facts/finetuning/{finetune_gpu,finetune_api}.py`, `false_facts/evaluations/`, `universe_creation_streamlit/app.py` | Python>=3.11, torch>=2.5.1, transformers4.47.1, PEFT>=.14, safety-tooling and API credentials for generation/hosted FT. Broad multimedia dependencies need not be installed for a minimal port. No root LICENSE found. |\n| [believe-it-or-not](https://github.com/safety-research/believe-it-or-not), `believe-it-or-not/` | SDF versus prompt/mechanistic editing, generality/robustness/probing evaluations for direction3 | `science_synth_facts/synth_doc_generation.py`, `