n/ | Train405/dev115/test1,879 =2,399;0.46MB JSONL | Main hypothesis-specific pilot suite |','', 'All row counts are locally measured. Blank WikiText rows are retained and counted separately. Schemas, provenance, licenses, loading and exact download commands: [datasets/README.md](datasets/README.md). Small actual samples are tracked; raw data are Git-ignored. CounterFact license is unspecified in the hosted card. Arithmetic suite semantics are explicit and not a globally coherent replacement for arithmetic.','', '## Code','', '| Repository | Pinned commit | Local path | Purpose |','|---|---|---|---|']\npurpose={'model-editing-ft':'Single-edit loss/trainer and replay','RippleEdits':'Conditional ripple evaluation and benchmark','rome':'Rank-one baseline and CounterFact evaluator','AlphaEdit':'Null-space preservation comparator','false-facts':'Original SDF data/training/evaluation','believe-it-or-not':'Generality, robustness and belief-depth pipeline'}\nfor x in repos:lines.append(f\\\"| [{x['name']}]({x['url']}) | \"'`{x['\"'commit']}\"'` | {x['\"'path']}/ | {purpose[x['name']]} |\\\")\nlines+=['','Readmes/dependencies/entrypoints inspected; no heavy packages, models, submodules or paid APIs installed/run. [code/README.md](code/README.md) describes version conflicts, GPU requirements, licenses and adaptation points. Clones preserve upstream embedded files; experiment-ready datasets are separated under datasets/.','', '## Search and selection','', 'Paper-finder diligent search was used first, after installing its missing httpx dependency in the fresh uv environment. Search terms covered knowledge-editing locality, counterfactual arithmetic, ripple effects, belief adoption, SDF and arithmetic mechanisms. Full output: paper_search.json; per-attempt results: notes/search_downloads.jsonl and notes/search_downloads_retry.jsonl. ArXiv/official paper pages, Semantic Scholar, GitHub and Hugging Face supplemented the search; broad web queries also checked Scholar/Papers with Code. No private dataset or Kaggle credential was needed.','', 'Every returned candidate received a download attempt; failed Semantic Scholar retrievals were retried through arXiv title matching. Rate limiting (429), gateway/API failures and unmatched titles prevented196 supplementary entries from resolving to local PDFs. [notes/search_access.csv](notes/search_access.csv) reconciles failures against PDFs already downloaded independently. Missing abstracts were screened by title; the acquired SSS abstract was read from its first PDF page. This is a structured resource search, not a registered systematic review or exhaustive current-SOTA claim.','', 'All eight user-specified arXiv PDFs were deep-read using three-page chunks; all chunks, including appendices, were visually inspected. The highest-ranked Shattering paper also received complete chunk review. The three specified web articles were fully read. The linked90-page Believe paper was main-text reviewed only. [notes/chunk_reading_log.md](notes/chunk_reading_log.md) preserves immediate notes. Broader downloaded papers were screened, not uniformly deep-read.','', '## Experiment handoff','', 'The evidence-weighted ranking and rejected directions are fixed in [planning.md](planning.md): (1) preservation-constrained parametric editing; (2) exact and semantic routing boundaries; (3) training breadth versus depth of adoption. These share one frozen evaluation suite. Additional papers do not expand the implementation search space.','', 'Start by checking model/tokenizer revisions, hardware/access and base arithmetic competence; then cache base outputs/logits. Adapt the single-edit FT loss first, include unchanged/sham/true-fact controls, and compare methods at matched efficacy using dev-selected hyperparameters. Keep exact-string routing labeled as a wrapper control. Use repeated seeds and family-aware uncertainty. Report desired semantic propagation separately from harmful preservation failures.','', 'Primary measures: exact efficacy, paraphrase transfer, near/far/operator agreement and accuracy, paired downstream ordinary/edited-rule agreement, unrelated factual/math behavior, full-distribution KL and held-out NLL, answer5 bias, parameter change and latency. Numeric AST oracles and lexical samples are ready; broad SDF corpora are intentionally not generated in resource gathering and require a matched-token generation protocol in direction3.','', '## Reproducibility and limitations','', 'Fresh .venv, pyproject.toml and uv.lock isolate resource dependencies. Run \"'`uv sync`, followed by dataset/repository scripts documented above. No conda or ambient research environment was used. All original PDFs parse; data hashes/row counts and git exclusions are verified in notes/resource_validation.json. Model weights, covariance matrices and large synthetic-document corpora are not downloaded; full published-scale replications therefore remain outside the ready-to-run resource set. The generated benchmark is deterministic but small/templated in semantic strata. Neither zero observed leakage nor a changed probe establishes universal isolation or genuine belief.'\"','', 'Pipeline state is preserved in STATE.md; only the resource_finder-owned notes are updated. Completion is signaled by .resource_finder_complete after final validation.']\n(R/'resources.md').write_text('\\\\n'.join(lines)+'\\\\n')\n# Add relevance to paper catalog without exposing long copied abstracts.\np=R/'papers/README.md';s=p.read_text();s+='\\\\n## Why each acquired paper was retained\\\\n\\\\n'\nfor x in ps:s+=f\\\"- \"'`{Path(x['\"'file']).name}\"'`: {info[Path(x['\"'file']).stem]}\\\\n\\\"\np.write_text(s)\nprint('Created resources.md and relevance annotations')\nPY\n.venv/bin/python scripts/build_resource_catalog.py\ncat >> .gitignore <<'EOF'\n\n# Resource-finder caches and shallow upstream checkouts (recreated by scripts)\n/code/*/\n/notes/rendered/\n/papers/pages/\nEOF\n.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('datasets/README.md');s=p.read_text().replace('one actual edit in \"'`ripple_sample.json`.'\"','one actual edit in \"'`ripple_sample.json`. Counts: popular885, random1,922, recent1,948 (4,755 total;42,395,155 bytes).'\"');p.write_text(s)\nPY\n.venv/bin/python scripts/update_state.py <<'EOF'\nPhases1–4 complete. Final synthesis in literature_review.md (about1,535 words), full reading notes in notes/chunk_reading_log.md; resources.md catalogs40 original PDFs,3 user-specified web articles,4 downloaded datasets plus1 generated suite, and6 pinned official repos. All specified resources acquired. Exactly3 directions retained in planning.md; no later expansion. Paper-finder233 candidates:37 available locally,196 supplemental PDFs unavailable after retries (notes/search_access.csv). Official RippleEdits release counts4,755 versus differing paper counts; CounterFact21,919; arithmetic2,399. Dataset manifests and code requirements documented.\nNext Phase5: validate all original/chunk PDFs, data schemas/hashes/splits, code commits/entrypoints, dependency isolation and git exclusions; then write completion marker. Remaining limitations are access gaps in supplementary literature, unspecified CounterFact data license, no downloaded model/covariance/SDF corpora, and untested CUDA/API runtime compatibility. No model experiments or universal isolation claim.\nEOF\npwd; cat STATE.md\"","aggregated_output":"/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-2d1a-codex-gpt-6-astra\nCreated resources.md and relevance annotations\n/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-2d1a-codex-gpt-6-astra\n# Research State\n\n- Current phase: `resource_finder`\n- Pipeline completed: `False`\n\n## Previous phases\n\nNo prior phases completed.\n\n## Current phase context\n\n- Phase: `resource_finder`\n- Status: `in_progress`\n- Started: `2026-10-04T08:29:37.424031Z`\n- Next steps:\n  - Review the literature and resource catalog before running experiments.\n\n## Workspace check\n\n- Root: `/workspaces/isolating-knowledge-updates-2d1a-codex-gpt-6-astra`\n- Directory usable: `True`\n\n## Output validation\n\nNo phase output validation recorded yet.\n\n## Agent notes\n\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START -->\n### resource_finder\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_START:resource_finder -->\nPhases1–4 complete. Final synthesis in literature_review.md (about1,535 words), full reading notes in notes/chunk_reading_log.md; resources.md catalogs40 original PDFs,3 user-specified web articles,4 downloaded datasets plus1 generated suite, and6 pinned official repos. All specified resources acquired. Exactly3 directions retained in planning.md; no later expansion. Paper-finder233 candidates:37 available locally,196 supplemental PDFs unavailable after retries (notes/search_access.csv). Official RippleEdits release counts4,755 versus differing paper counts; CounterFact21,919; arithmetic2,399. Dataset manifests and code requirements documented.\nNext Phase5: validate all original/chunk PDFs, data schemas/hashes/splits, code commits/entrypoints, dependency isolation and git exclusions; then write completion marker. Remaining limitations are access gaps in supplementary literature, unspecified CounterFact data license, no downloaded model/covariance/SDF corpora, and untested CUDA/API runtime compatibility. No model experiments or universal isolation claim.\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END:resource_finder -->\n\n### Legacy notes\nNo phase notes recorded yet.\n\n<!-- NEURICO_AGENT_NOTES_END -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
